      "settings.embeddings.quickSetupFreeTitle": "Free alternatives:",
      "settings.embeddings.quickSetupFreeDesc": "Local providers run embedding models at no cost. Install a local inference server, pull nomic-embed-text, and add it as a local embedding model above.",
      "settings.embeddings.infoIndexTitle": "Semantic index",
      "settings.embeddings.infoIndexBody": 'The semantic index reads all your notes, breaks them into small sections, and converts each section into a mathematical representation of its meaning (called an "embedding"). When you ask the agent a question, it searches for notes with similar meaning rather than just matching words. This makes the agent much better at finding relevant context in your vault.',
      "settings.embeddings.infoCheckpointTitle": "Checkpoint interval",
      "settings.embeddings.infoCheckpointBody": "The indexer saves a checkpoint to disk every n files. If indexing is interrupted (app closed, error), the next run resumes from the last checkpoint \u2014 only unindexed or modified files are processed. A smaller interval loses less progress on interruption but writes to disk more often. 10\u201330 is recommended for most vaults.",
      "settings.embeddings.infoHydeTitle": "`HyDE`",
      "settings.embeddings.infoHydeBody": 'Hypothetical document embeddings is a technique that improves semantic search recall. Instead of embedding your query directly, the agent first asks the model to write a short note that would answer your question. That hypothetical text is then embedded and used for the search. This is especially helpful for vague queries like "what are my goals?" where a direct embedding might not match well. The downside is one extra model call per search.',
      "settings.embeddings.infoAutoChangeTitle": "Auto-index on change",
      "settings.embeddings.infoAutoChangeBody": "When enabled, every file you edit is re-embedded 2 seconds after you stop typing. This works well with API-based embedding models.",
      "settings.embeddings.infoAutoStrategyTitle": "Auto-index strategy",
      "settings.embeddings.infoAutoStrategyBody": `"on startup" rebuilds the index every time Obsidian opens \u2014 keeps the index fresh but adds a few seconds to startup time for large vaults. "on mode switch" rebuilds whenever you switch agent modes, useful if each mode works with different parts of your vault. "never" means you control when to rebuild using the "force reindex vault" option in the chat's ellipsis menu.`,
      "settings.embeddings.infoExcludedTitle": "Excluded folders",
      "settings.embeddings.infoExcludedBody": "Use this to skip folders that contain files you do not want the agent to search through \u2014 for example, attachment folders full of images or `PDFs`, template folders, or private journals. Enter the folder path relative to your vault root, one per line.",
      "settings.embeddings.riskNote": "Risk: this setting may slow down your vault performance or freeze Obsidian.",
